.TH "GIT-BUG" "1" "Apr 2019" "Generated from git-bug's source code" ""

.SH NAME
git-bug-pr-review - Submit a review of a pull request


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgit-bug pr review PR_ID [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Submit a review of a pull request. With neither --message nor --at, and unless --non-interactive is given, the editor opens on the diff of the pull request: write the summary above the diff, and each comment on the lines right under the diff line it is about.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--approve\fP[=false]
	Approve the changes

.PP
\fB--request-changes\fP[=false]
	Request changes

.PP
\fB-m\fP, \fB--message\fP=""
	Provide the review summary from the command line

.PP
\fB--at\fP=[]
	Comment on a line of the head commit, as PATH:LINE:MESSAGE. Can be repeated

.PP
\fB--non-interactive\fP[=false]
	Do not ask for user input

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for review


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--no-colors\fP[=]
	Do not color the output


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBgit-bug-pr(1)\fP
